/* ============================================================
   SECTION 4: Pivot Tables
   ============================================================ */
+ '<h2 class="l-title">4. Pivot Tables</h2>'

+ '<div class="calc-highlight"><strong>Pivot tables reshape data from long to wide format.</strong> Instead of groupby + aggregation + manual reshaping, <code>pd.pivot_table()</code> does it all in one step. It creates a cross-tabulation with aggregated values -- like Excel\'s PivotTable feature.</div>'

+ '<div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-label"><span>PYTHON</span><button class="copy-btn" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest(\'.code-wrap\').querySelector(\'code\').textContent)">COPY</button></div><pre class="code-block"><code><span class="kw">import</span> pandas <span class="kw">as</span> pd\n<span class="kw">import</span> numpy <span class="kw">as</span> np\n\n<span class="cm"># Larger dataset for pivot tables</span>\nnp.random.<span class="fn">seed</span>(<span class="num">42</span>)\ndf = pd.<span class="fn">DataFrame</span>({\n    <span class="str">"student"</span>: [<span class="str">"Alice"</span>,<span class="str">"Alice"</span>,<span class="str">"Alice"</span>,<span class="str">"Bob"</span>,<span class="str">"Bob"</span>,<span class="str">"Bob"</span>,\n                <span class="str">"Carol"</span>,<span class="str">"Carol"</span>,<span class="str">"Carol"</span>,<span class="str">"Dave"</span>,<span class="str">"Dave"</span>,<span class="str">"Dave"</span>],\n    <span class="str">"subject"</span>: [<span class="str">"NLP"</span>,<span class="str">"CV"</span>,<span class="str">"DL"</span>]*<span class="num">4</span>,\n    <span class="str">"semester"</span>: [<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,<span class="str">"Fall"</span>,\n                 <span class="str">"Spring"</span>,<span class="str">"Spring"</span>,<span class="str">"Spring"</span>,<span class="str">"Spring"</span>,<span class="str">"Spring"</span>,<span class="str">"Spring"</span>],\n    <span class="str">"score"</span>:   [<span class="num">92</span>,<span class="num">85</span>,<span class="num">88</span>,<span class="num">76</span>,<span class="num">90</span>,<span class="num">82</span>,<span class="num">95</span>,<span class="num">78</span>,<span class="num">91</span>,<span class="num">80</span>,<span class="num">88</span>,<span class="num">85</span>]\n})\n\n<span class="cm"># Basic pivot table: students as rows, subjects as columns</span>\npivot = pd.<span class="fn">pivot_table</span>(\n    df,\n    values=<span class="str">"score"</span>,\n    index=<span class="str">"student"</span>,\n    columns=<span class="str">"subject"</span>,\n    aggfunc=<span class="str">"mean"</span>\n)\n<span class="fn">print</span>(pivot)\n<span class="cm"># subject   CV    DL   NLP</span>\n<span class="cm"># student</span>\n<span class="cm"># Alice    85.0  88.0  92.0</span>\n<span class="cm"># Bob      90.0  82.0  76.0</span>\n<span class="cm"># Carol    78.0  91.0  95.0</span>\n<span class="cm"># Dave     88.0  85.0  80.0</span>\n\n<span class="cm"># With margins (totals) and multiple aggfuncs</span>\npivot2 = pd.<span class="fn">pivot_table</span>(\n    df,\n    values=<span class="str">"score"</span>,\n    index=<span class="str">"student"</span>,\n    columns=<span class="str">"subject"</span>,\n    aggfunc=[<span class="str">"mean"</span>, <span class="str">"count"</span>],\n    margins=<span class="kw">True</span>,              <span class="cm"># add row/column totals</span>\n    margins_name=<span class="str">"Total"</span>\n)\n<span class="fn">print</span>(pivot2)\n\n<span class="cm"># Multi-level pivot: semester + subject</span>\npivot3 = pd.<span class="fn">pivot_table</span>(\n    df,\n    values=<span class="str">"score"</span>,\n    index=<span class="str">"student"</span>,\n    columns=[<span class="str">"semester"</span>, <span class="str">"subject"</span>],\n    aggfunc=<span class="str">"mean"</span>,\n    fill_value=<span class="num">0</span>                <span class="cm"># fill missing combos with 0</span>\n)\n<span class="fn">print</span>(pivot3)</code></pre></div>'

+ '<div class="calc-steps">'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">values</div><div class="step-detail">The column to aggregate (what you are measuring). Example: <code>"score"</code>.</div></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">index</div><div class="step-detail">What becomes the <strong>rows</strong> of the pivot table. Can be a single column or a list for hierarchical rows.</div></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">columns</div><div class="step-detail">What becomes the <strong>columns</strong> of the pivot table. The unique values of this column become new column headers.</div></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">aggfunc</div><div class="step-detail">How to aggregate when there are multiple values. Default is <code>"mean"</code>. Can be a string, function, list, or dict.</div></div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">margins</div><div class="step-detail">Set <code>margins=True</code> to add row/column totals (like the "Grand Total" row/column in Excel).</div></div></div>'
+ '</div>'

